  "worked_solution": "Previously, we found that $\\overset{\u2194}{AB}$ has equation\n\n$$\ny=-3x+7.\n$$\n\nAt the $x$-intercept, the $y$-coordinate is equal to $0.$ So, we can substitute $y=0$ into the equation and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x+7 \\\\ 0 & =-3x+7 \\\\ -7 & =-3x \\\\ \\frac{-7}{-3} & =\\frac{-3x}{-3} \\\\ \\frac{7}{3} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $x=\\frac{7}{3}.$ The coordinates of the $x$-intercept are $(\\frac{7}{3},0).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
